    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on stolen base upside and favorable platoon matchups. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) anchors the outfield, benefiting from a 14% boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage against Luis Castillo and a prime leadoff spot, making him our highest-projected asset for speed and efficiency. **Trea Turner** (74.57) and **Kyle Schwarber** (73.46) follow closely in the lineup against the favorable Junk; while both face slight situational downgrades, their roles at the top of the order provide immense volume for R and RBI production. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** (70.15) remains a must-start, as his ability to leverage a 12% SP skill advantage against Young allows him to transcend the park factor drag to provide our most potent middle-order power threat.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the roster involves the utility spots, where **Caleb Durbin** (67.03) narrowly edged out the rest of the fringe starters. **Durbin** carries a massive 19% SP skill boost against Bratt, providing the highest ceiling among our MI options. Conversely, **Lars Nootbaar** (42.83) sits firmly in the marginal category today; while his park factor is positive, his placement in the 8th hole and a unfavorable dynamic platoon split against Gamboa significantly stifle his projected floor. We are opting to roll with **Nootbaar** over the bench depth solely for the volume, as our high-upside bench options like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Gary Sanchez** are all unavailable due to scheduled off-days.\n\nManagerial caution is advised regarding **Dillon Dingler** (45.71) and **Chase Meidroth** (51.80). **Dingler** faces a difficult matchup against Mlodzinski, and while he is currently a marginal start, his efficiency score is suppressed by defensive variables. **Meidroth** draws the toughest assignment of the day against Imanaga; while the leadoff spot offers a 10% boost, the lack of positive SP variables keeps him near the baseline. As we monitor the wire for late-breaking lineup changes involving **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, or **Pedro Ramirez**, ensure your game caps are managed\u2014we are prioritizing high-efficiency starts to maintain our Roto lead without burning through our remaining seasonal allotment.",
